    <!-- Translation notes -->
    <h3>Translation notes</h3>
    <p>OpenIntro builds inference from the sampling distribution of the sample proportion, then generalizes. We use the sample mean for clarity. The original covers decision errors with medical testing analogies and uses simulation to build intuition for sampling distributions. With many degrees of freedom, t critical values approach normal critical values. The examples here use the t-distribution because the population standard deviation is estimated from ten observations; Ch. 7 develops this method further.</p>

